                            <tr><td><strong>Trade Line</strong></td><td>A credit account listed on a credit report.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Derogatory</strong></td><td>Negative information on a credit report (e.g., late payments, collections, bankruptcies).</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Foreclosure</strong></td><td>Legal process where a lender takes possession of a property due to non-payment.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Short Sale</strong></td><td>Sale of a property for less than the amount owed, with lender approval.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Deed-in-Lieu</strong></td><td>Borrower voluntarily transfers property to lender to avoid foreclosure.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Chapter 7</strong></td><td>Liquidation bankruptcy – debts are discharged; property may be sold.</td></tr>
