                    <table id="termTableTRID">
                        <thead><tr><th style="width:25%;">Term</th><th>Definition</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><strong>TRID</strong></td><td>TILA-RESPA Integrated Disclosure – CFPB rule combining mortgage disclosures.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>TILA</strong></td><td>Truth in Lending Act – federal law requiring disclosure of credit terms.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>RESPA</strong></td><td>Real Estate Settlement Procedures Act – federal law governing settlement practices.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>CFPB</strong></td><td>Consumer Financial Protection Bureau – agency that created and enforces TRID.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>LE</strong></td><td>Loan Estimate – disclosure given within 3 business days of application.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>CD</strong></td><td>Closing Disclosure – final disclosure received at least 3 business days before consummation.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>GFE</strong></td><td>Good Faith Estimate – old form replaced by the LE.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>HUD-1</strong></td><td>HUD Settlement Statement – old form replaced by the CD.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>APR</strong></td><td>Annual Percentage Rate – the cost of credit expressed as a yearly rate.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Finance Charge</strong></td><td>The dollar amount the credit will cost the borrower.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Consummation</strong></td><td>The date the borrower signs the security instrument and note.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Business Day (LE)</strong></td><td>A day the creditor is open for substantially all business functions (Saturdays usually excluded).</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Business Day (CD)</strong></td><td>All calendar days except Sundays and legal holidays (Saturdays count).</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Intent to Proceed</strong></td><td>Borrower's written intent to move forward; required before collecting fees (except credit report).</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Change of Circumstance</strong></td><td>A valid event allowing redisclosure of the LE (e.g., rate lock, appraisal change).</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Zero Tolerance</strong></td><td>Fees that cannot increase (e.g., lender fees, transfer taxes).</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>10% Cumulative Tolerance</strong></td><td>Fees that can increase up to 10% in aggregate (e.g., recording fees).</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Redisclosure</strong></td><td>Issuing a new LE or CD due to a valid change; CD triggers new 3-day waiting period.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>NMLS ID</strong></td><td>Nationwide Multistate Licensing System ID – license number for loan originators and lenders.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>MIC</strong></td><td>Mortgage Insurance Certificate – number shown on the CD.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>E-SIGN</strong></td><td>Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce Act – governs electronic delivery.</td></tr>
